   253	The fraction is `~ C(c,i)(i!)^2 n^{-2i}`: **inverse-polynomial in `n` at fixed homological
   254	degree `i`**, exponentially small only as `i` grows. Contrast the normalised Hilbert
   255	function, `rho^{codim}` with `rho ~ 0.75` (applications memo F2, caution 1), exponentially
   256	small for every square system. Arm B's observable survives F2 where arm A's does not — at
   257	the price of an `n^{-2i}` precision target, i.e. `n^{4i}` samples at fixed `i`.
