   433	  `c_k^†|S> = (-1)^{#{l in S : l<k}}|S ∪ {k}>` for `k not in S`, else 0; fermion number
   434	  `F̂ = sum_k c_k^† c_k`. Pitfall: the sign is not decorative — dropping it breaks `Q^2 = 0`
   435	  (mutation M3).
   436	- **D-koszul-supercharge.** `Q = sum_k a_k ⊗ c_k^†` on `F ⊗ Lambda(C^{n+1})`
   437	  (D-mode-operators, D-fermionic-modes); `Q^2 = 0` exactly; carries block `(i,N)` to
   438	  `(i+1,N-1)` and preserves `j = N+i`. Restriction `Q_W = Q(P_0 ⊗ 1)` is well defined
   439	  because `(I_N)^perp` is `a_k`-invariant (D-inverse-system). Pitfall: `Q^†` does **not**
   440	  restrict; its restriction is `sum_k Z_k ⊗ c_k`, D-compressed-multiplication.
   441	- **D-betti-laplacian.** `L_W = Q_W Q_W^† + Q_W^† Q_W` on `(I_N)^perp ⊗ Lambda^i`; equals
   442	  `(N+i)1 - X X^†` with `X = (P_0⊗1) Q (1 - P_0⊗1)`; `0 <= L_W <= (N+i)1`. Pitfall:
   443	  `L_W != (P_0⊗1) L (P_0⊗1)`, which is the scalar `(N+i)`.
   444	- **D-graded-betti-number.** `beta_{i,j}(R/I) = dim Tor_i^R(R/I, C)_j`; `beta_{i,j} = 0`
   445	  for `i > n+1` or `j - i > reg(R/I)`; `beta_{1,j}` = minimal generators of `I` in degree
