     4	
     5	# `checkers/` — red-capable checker suite
     6	
     7	Sixteen checkers turning the seed numerics
     8	(`seed/analysis-2026-09-01/numerics/`) into tests that can **fail**. Each one
     9	states at the top which seed claim it tests (report section plus the numbered
    10	Fact / Prop / Conjecture), exits `0` only when every tested property holds
    11	within a stated tolerance, and exits `1` with a printed reason otherwise. Every
    12	checker has a recorded red mutation in `MUTATIONS.md`.
    13	
    14	The seed report is a **proposer document**, not established truth. Nothing here
    15	promotes any of its claims; a PASS says "the stated numerical property holds on
    16	the tested range at the stated tolerance", nothing more. In particular all the
    17	Section 8 items remain conjectures: what is checked is the *numerical evidence
    18	the report cites for them*, not the conjectures.
    19	
    20	## Running
    21	
    22	```bash
    23	cd checkers
    24	timeout 2400 ./run_all.sh                       # all 16, PASS/FAIL + wall time
    25	timeout 600  ./run_all.sh check_fact72_takagi.py  # a subset
    26	timeout 1800 python3 run_mutations.py           # the red mutations (MUTATIONS.md)
    27	timeout 300  python3 explore/explore_dynrange.py  # exploration, no exit code
    28	```
    29	
    30	`run_all.sh` runs every checker under `timeout` with a per-script budget (about
    31	5x the measured wall time), prints PASS/FAIL and wall time per checker, writes
    32	per-checker output to `logs/`, and exits nonzero if any checker fails.
    33	
    34	Python on this machine: 3.12.3, numpy 2.4.6, scipy 1.17.0, sympy 1.14.0. All
    35	three are present; nothing is missing. `scipy` is used only by
    36	`check_task8_cnf.py` (sparse `a(f)`, deflated LOBPCG); `sympy` only by
    37	`check_task1_conic.py` and `check_task2_hilbert.py` (exact symbolic ranks and
    38	the symbolic form of Fact 2.3).
    39	
    40	## Discipline (rk-light L4)
    41	
    42	- **No bare `assert`.** `grep -rn assert *.py` finds only two occurrences, both
    43	  inside comments/docstrings. `python3 -O check_*.py` behaves exactly like
    44	  `python3 check_*.py`; spot-checked on three checkers.
    45	- **Fail-fast with a printed reason.** `checkharness.py` raises `CheckFailure`
    46	  on the first violation; the last line of output is always `FAIL: <reason>`
    47	  (or `PASS: <k> checks in <t>s wall`). Exit `2` is reserved for "the checker
    48	  could not run at all" (unexpected exception).
    49	- **Bounded.** Every checker declares its dimension caps at the top of the file
    50	  and every run in `run_all.sh` and `run_mutations.py` goes under `timeout`.
    51	- **Seed is read-only.** `bf.py`, `ideals.py` and `gaps.py` here are byte-for-
    52	  byte copies of `seed/analysis-2026-09-01/numerics/`; the task scripts were
    53	  copied and refactored for exit codes with their numerical content preserved
    54	  (same ideals, same seeds, same N ranges except where a cap is listed below).
    55	
    56	## Conventions
    57	
    58	`definitions/definitions.md` is the single source (L2). Objects used here:
    59	`D-fock-space`, `D-fock-basis`, `D-annihilation-of-form`, `D-hamiltonian`,
    60	`D-macaulay-matrix`, `D-macaulay-gap`, `D-hilbert-function`, `D-inverse-system`,
    61	`D-toric-ideal`, `D-boolean-ideal`, `D-clause-ideal`, `D-initial-ideal`,
    62	`D-groebner-deformation-path`, `D-coherent-state`, `D-coherent-gram-matrix`,
    63	`D-multidegree-sector`, `D-cone`, `D-kostlan-random-form`,
    64	`D-takagi-factorisation`.
    65	
    66	**Departure from convention C5.** C5 fixes gap statements to *unit
    67	Bombieri-Weyl* generators. The seed's numerical survey does not use that
    68	normalisation (this is OPEN-1 in the definitions register), and this suite
    69	reproduces the seed, so every `Delta_N` here is the gap of the presentation
    70	**as written** (unit coefficients on the monomials of each generator). Every
    71	checker docstring repeats this. Consequences that matter: `Delta_N` of the
    72	conic is `N+1` in this normalisation, not the unit-BW value; the boolean
    73	`Delta = 2` is likewise presentation-dependent. Convention C9 (Takagi values
    74	written `tau_j`, `tau_min`) is followed in `check_fact72_takagi.py`.
