   101	## Exploration scripts (excluded from `run_all.sh`)
   102	
   103	- `explore/explore_dynrange.py` — part (C) of the seed's `task3b_hard.py`
   104	  (coefficient dynamic range `eps` in a single bilinear generator). **The seed
   105	  report states no claim that these numbers support.** The nearest statement,
   106	  Sect. 7's "`(f_1, f_1 + eps f_2)` ... has `Delta_N = O(eps^2)`", is about a
   107	  two-generator tuple with a near-redundancy; this script perturbs a *single*
   108	  generator and the ideal itself changes with `eps`. The observed behaviour is
   109	  the opposite of a collapse: `Delta` is *smallest* at `eps = 1` (0.0833 at
   110	  `m = 6`) and saturates at the `eps -> 0` value (0.1340) already by
   111	  `eps = 1e-2`. There is no property here whose violation would refute anything
   112	  in the report, so wrapping it in an exit code would be theatre. It is kept as
   113	  an exploration script and excluded from `run_all.sh`.
   114	
   115	Everything else in the seed's `numerics/` supports at least one checkable
   116	property and has been promoted to a checker.
