     9	## The idea (orchestrator's working formulation; attack it as well as develop it)
    10	For a homogeneous ideal I in R = C[z_0..z_n], the graded Betti numbers beta_{i,j}(R/I) = dim Tor_i^R(R/I, C)_j are the homology of the Koszul complex of R/I with respect to the variables. In the Fock model, (R/I)_N is identified (D-inverse-system, §2 rows) with ker H_N = I_N^perp, and I^perp is closed under every annihilation operator a_k = partial_k (since <partial_k g, h> = <g, z_k h>). So on the graded space ker H (x) Lambda(C^{n+1}) (bosonic ground space tensor fermionic exterior algebra) the operator Q = sum_k a_k (x) c_k^dag satisfies Q^2 = 0 EXACTLY (the a_k commute, the c_k^dag anticommute), with no compression needed. The supersymmetric Laplacian L = Q Q^dag + Q^dag Q is block-diagonal in (fermion number i, total boson degree), and by Hodge theory its nullity in the block (i, N) equals a graded Betti number of R/I (fix the exact index convention: which (i,j) of beta_{i,j}, and whether this is Koszul homology of R/I or, by duality, of the inverse system). This gives a Hamiltonian, local in the same sense as H_N (D-k-body), whose ground-state degeneracy per block is the Betti table. No such statement is in the seed or the DAG.
    11	
    12	## Task
    13	1. **Make it precise.** State the complex, the grading, the exact identification nullity(L restricted to block (i,N)) = beta_{i,?}(R/I), and prove it at the level of an addressable sketch (numbered steps, ASSUME/PROVE, each leaf citing a D-id or a C-id; law L3). Cover: (a) L acts on the FULL Fock (x) Lambda space too, and the full Koszul complex of R is exact except in degree 0, so ker L on the full space is trivial except for the vacuum: the Betti information appears only after restriction to ker H, i.e. after projection with P_0 (the seed's ground-space projector, D-projectors). Say exactly what operator a quantum algorithm would block-encode: is it P_0 L P_0 (with P_0 = P_0^{(N)} (x) 1), and does its nullity on range(P_0 (x) 1) equal the Betti number, or do you need L built from compressed operators (D-compressed-multiplication)? (b) The relation to D-syzygy-module (first syzygies are beta_{2,*} of R/I, or beta_{1,*} of I) and to C-052 / §5 rows that already treat Syz(I)_N. (c) The normalisation: what is ||L||, and what is the 'Betti gap' g_{i,N}, the smallest nonzero eigenvalue of L in block (i,N)? Is it related to the Macaulay gap Delta_N (D-macaulay-gap) or is it a genuinely new parameter?
    14	2. **Numerics** (checkers/explore/koszul_laplacian.py, on checkers/bf.py, exit 0, bounded by `timeout 900`, print tables). For at least: the twisted cubic (2x2 minors of a 2x3 matrix in P^3, Betti table beta_{1,2}=3, beta_{2,3}=2), a complete intersection of two quadrics in P^3 (beta_{1,2}=2, beta_{2,4}=1), one monomial ideal with a non-trivial Betti table (e.g. (x^2, xy, y^2) or the Stanley-Reisner ideal of a small complex) and, if it fits, the rational normal quartic. Compute: (a) the nullity of L per block (i,N) for N up to the stable range and compare with the Betti table computed independently over Q by exact rank (rank_mod_p on Koszul matrices, or sympy), pass/fail per block; (b) the Betti gap g_{i,N} versus N for each i; (c) the normalised Betti fraction beta_{i,j} / dim(block (i,N)) and its decay with N and n, since a DQC1-style estimate (D-dqc1-style-estimate) resolves only additive precision, and the applications memo's codimension law (cautions 1-2) says most normalised observables are exponentially small.
    15	3. **Against the north star** (PRD §2, all five criteria). Problem statement with input model; classical baseline from classical-landscape §10 (block Wiedemann, Schreyer, stochastic trace filtering) AND the dequantization literature for exactly this shape of algorithm: Lloyd-Garnerone-Zanardi quantum TDA (arXiv:1408.3106), Berry et al 'Analyzing prospects for quantum advantage in topological data analysis' (arXiv:2209.13581), Apers-Gribling-Sen-Szabo classical Betti-number estimation (arXiv:2211.09618), Schmidhuber-Lloyd complexity limits (arXiv:2209.14286), Crichigno-Kohler clique homology QMA1-hardness (resolve the id), Gyurik-Cade-Dunjko (arXiv:2005.02607). Resolve every id. State plainly whether a normalised-Betti-fraction estimator at additive precision 1/poly is dequantized by Apers et al-style Chebyshev/Krylov methods given sparse access to L, and what promise (Betti gap, fraction not exponentially small) would be needed for it not to be. Hardware hook: fermion-boson Hamiltonians (Bose-Fermi Hubbard, or a Jordan-Wigner fermion register plus the seed's bosonic modes); say what the smallest demonstration would be.
    16	4. **Output**: scouting/koszul-betti.md, 250-450 lines, sections 'Statement and sketch' (Lamport-numbered), 'Numerics' (tables pasted, with the command line that regenerates them), 'Against the north star' (criteria 1-5 each answered in one paragraph), 'Killers' (numbered K-KB1..), 'Proposed definitions' (register format, e.g. D-koszul-supercharge, D-betti-laplacian, D-betti-gap), 'Proposed claim rows' (exact statements with quantifiers, status CONJECTURE unless the numerics REFUTE, ids C-NEW-KB-<NAME>, depends-on with D-ids and C-ids), 'Questions for TJO'. Finish within about 45 minutes of wall time; if the numerics run long, shrink N.

