  3934	## Critical claims for the north star
  3935	
  3936	The eight rows whose promotion (or refutation) would most move the campaign, with what a
  3937	critic must recompute. Ordered by expected movement, not by id.
  3938	
  3939	1. **C-124 (Conjecture 8.1: distance-to-ideal estimation is BQP-hard and in BQP).**
  3940	   The only candidate BQP-hardness statement for an algebraic-geometry problem in the whole
  3941	   seed. A critic must recompute both endpoint overlaps `<f_±|P_0|f_±>` of C-126 for a
  3942	   concrete small circuit, confirm their difference is `2 Re<y|U|0>/(T+1)`, and — the part
  3943	   no round has checked — verify that the Feynman–Kitaev Hamiltonian really is realised by
  3944	   multilinear generators of degree `≤ 5` in the `(1,...,1)` sector with the claimed
  3945	   sector-restricted gap `Ω(T^{-2})`. Blockers: C-125 (the C-054 oracles are asserted, not
  3946	   constructed); C-239 and C-253 record the two ways the draft got this wrong.
  3947	
